# Build artefacts
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
*.pyc

# Tool caches — nothing here belongs in a distributed artefact
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.vulture_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Run output
logs/
results/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# Browser download artefacts. A commit on this branch picked up a bare
# `download` file (a copy of this .gitignore) and `README (1).md` (a
# copy of docs/README.md) — both the shape a browser produces when
# saving a file that already exists locally.
download
*\ (1).*
*\ (2).*
*.download

# Source files loose at the repository root. The package lives in
# src/qrp/, docs/, study/, tests/ and tools/; a .py or .sql at the root
# is a stray copy, and a STALE one is worse than a duplicate — a commit
# here carried 83 flattened copies that were several changes behind the
# real tree, so reading them gave the wrong answer.
/*.py
/*.sql
/*.json
!package.py

# Images: the terminal UI renders are reproducible with
# `export_screenshot()` and are not kept in the repository.
*.svg
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
